title Mycelium Pledge r3 — the two-phase verdict reads across a Knot (a pledge kept after the cut)
prompt remember/loop card: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think r1 and r2 landed and pushed both remotes. Continuing the Pledge arc — r3 makes the corpus a Knot plus its live suffix, mirroring purse_knot carried from a single balance column to balance + reserved and open pledges. A ledger a family runs for years does not carry its whole past unbroken.
think Read the mirror purse_knot.rye in full and cord_knot's seal_dag/verify. The honest seam: cord_knot.Knot seals fold's GLOBAL supply law (issued/taxed/stars), not who holds what or which pledges stand open. So a PledgeKnot carries two things across the cut — the Knot (integrity-sealed supply, issued == total_issued) and the prefix verdict's accounts and open pledges (the map the FoldState omits). seal_dag runs fold.fold_fact which treats EVERY kind_tax as a global supply drain, so a reserve-and-resolve PAIR in one prefix would double-count taxed and overdraw; the fix is structural — keep the pledge ONE kind_tax fact in the sealed prefix and put the resolution in the live suffix, which is exactly where the contest belongs.
think This gave the truest crux for two-phase across a checkpoint: a pledge and its resolution can stand far apart in time, even across a pruning cut. Genesis 100 to Alice; Alice PLEDGES it to Bob inside the sealed prefix (reserved, not moved); after the past is tied off she POSTS it in the live suffix and the reserved hundred reaches Bob — a promise made before the cut, kept after it. A VOID in the suffix releases it back to Alice instead. Both resolutions read across the cut, proven.
obs GREEN first pass. continue_pledge seeds a Ledger from the prefix map and folds the suffix through the shared pledge.fold_pledge; pledges_match proves the full Cord and the Knot-continued verdict never drift (pledges, settlements, balances, reserves — position not compared, local to the live epoch). Conservation of balance + reserved holds past the cut. Three integrity refusals hold: a corrupt Knot (issued+1) refuses KnotCorrupt before a fact is folded, a tampered suffix fact IdentityRefused, a post of a pledge the checkpoint never opened UnknownPledge. Witness GREEN (the Pledge and the Knot re-run their green binaries at the door), TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0.
loom witness=mycelium_pledge_knot_witness result=GREEN posted_across=1 released_across=1 conserved=100 refusals=3 no_drift=true
file mycelium/pledge_knot.rye r3 — seal_pledge + continue_pledge; a pledge opened before the cut honored/released after it; conservation across the cut
file tools/mycelium_pledge_knot_witness.rish witness — selftest + the Pledge and the Knot re-run their green binaries at the door
recommend keep-going Pledge r4 closes the arc (a real on-disk fixture true, app == awk, mirroring purse_true): a reproducible Cord record carrying a pledge opened then honored, read true against an independent awk. REMEMBER still ~40 commits stale — a remember/align pass is worth folding the whole Mycelium arc onto the card. A served pledge · per-account mint authority · breach renames (cairn-first) · deep debride · seed force-push stay Keaton's hand.
